# ── 3. §10b standing lessons ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
L10B='''- **(V198) Two lenses on one word: a gate can COUNT a family by name while a ruling PROTECTS it by section.** `g193`'s B3 counts prehab from a `PREHAB_NAMES` hand list; D47 protects prehab as `s.hip` sections, which `_protected` makes structurally untouchable by the trim. So B3 went red for "prehab fell 661" while D47's rail was provably byte-identical (3,072/tier on both artifacts) — the 661 were four names sitting in a leg accessory superset. **Before believing a gate's noun, find the code that owns the same noun and check they mean the same set.** This cost a wrong diagnosis relayed to Mario and a doctrine question posed on a false premise.
- **(V198) A floor inside a cap that must still reach cap does not reduce the debt, it MOVES it.** D85 forbade the trim its last hinge and the trim simply took the next-ranked candidate. Every proposed cure — making more rails ineligible — made the displaced total WORSE, because the protected items were the expensive ones and the loop then ate twice as many cheap ones (`_isHalf` charges holds at 0.5×). **Ruling a floor means ruling where the displaced sets come from, in the same ruling.** Corollary, now doctrine: revisit coverage on the POOL or COST side, never by adding another floor.
- **(V198) A red is not a count. `gate.sh` exits at the first failing gate in glob order, so fixing one red uncovers the next.** V198 went red three times on three different gates; the first red masked the other two for a full build cycle. **When a chain goes red, run every gate individually against both artifacts to enumerate the FULL red set before designing any fix** — otherwise each round costs a coach ruling, a builder pass and a gatekeeper pass to discover one more failure.
- **(V198) A confinement pinned to "byte-identical to the baseline" dies at the first ruled edit to what it guards.** D84's E5 asserted `capSessionBudget` never changes; D85 ruled that it must. Re-pin such a gate to a DIGEST OF THE LICENSED TEXT, not to a baseline, and keep the old digest accepted only under a version predicate. The test that it still works is that a **comment-only** edit to the guarded function trips it: a confinement must detect an EDIT, not an outcome.
'''
s=rep('## 10b. Standing lessons (promoted out of the session digest)\n','## 10b. Standing lessons (promoted out of the session digest)\n'+L10B,'10b')

# ── 4. §11f rulings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
S11F='''### V198 — the last posterior item, and a ruling that had to survive its own measure pass (Mario: "Concur", "Concur with coach, option 1", "Go, coach and builder in parallel")

- **The budget may not spend the day's last hinge or hip extension (D85).** One candidate skip in `capSessionBudget`'s trim loop: `_pattern(it.name)` in `{hinge, hip_ext}` is ineligible when the day holds exactly one such item, counted live on `out` every iteration. **Unconditional by ruling** — not scoped to `cfg.injury`, region or equipment tier. Coach's reason is D84's: scoping would encode "the budget may spend a HEALTHY athlete's last posterior item", and the measured healthy + shoulder cost is 226 zero-posterior weeks, not a rounding error. Zero posterior chain on a day that loads the legs is not a coachable prescription for anyone.
- **`leg_iso` is excluded from the posterior set, and the exclusion is DOCTRINE-ONLY.** `EXLIB.leg_accessory` holds `Leg extension` and `Leg press` beside `Lying leg curl`, so `leg_iso` is not a posterior signal. Measured: folding it in changes 0/24 configs and 0/288 cells, because **0 of 864 budget invocations are ever offered a `leg_iso` item**. The gate records this in those words so no future session mistakes sabotage mutation M3 for evidence.
- **`<=1` is not a tuning constant.** It is the boundary between nonempty and empty, D50's boundary. The ruling's original justification was wrong and was corrected in session: nothing arrives at exactly 1 because the loop removes one item per iteration, so a day at 2 passes through 1 on its way to 0. The floor tests "is this the last one", read live, never precomputed.
- **The displacement is LICENSED, not fixed (option 1 over option 2).** Mario's lean was option 2 — make ruled-protected rails ineligible in the loop itself rather than watched by ratchets. Coach measured five variants and rejected it: the engine owns no prehab predicate (its nearest marker, `_pattern(name)===null`, is mostly the trunk family and zeroing it contradicts D48/D50), every in-doctrine variant made prehab worse, and the cap stopped binding on 1,001–4,905 day-builds. **Mario's recommendation was overruled by measurement, and he concurred.**
- **A licence is an equality, never a tolerance, and it self-expires (Mario, standing).** B3's D85 displacement is a hand-typed per-tier table asserted as `cand === base - table` on 6/6 tiers, armed only at `BASE_VER==='197' && !USE_FULL`, disarming at V199 when the displacement is already in the baseline. A licence that permits "up to" hides the second regression that walks in behind the first. It is paired with a **zero-residual confinement** (the fall outside the four named movements must be exactly 0 on 6/6) which is what gives it teeth, and with a **permanent, non-licence-bound `hip:true` rail-equality claim**, because D47's rail is what B3 exists to defend.
- **B4c's failure text was false as written, and the fix changed the CLAIM not the TEST.** It read "classes V192 never touched" while `allowed = baseKinds ? … : V192_NONOPT_CLASSES_WIDE` tests the LIVE baseline whenever one is passed — and V192 emptied `Leg` 8 times, as its own hand table says. Same species as the `g196_ledger` G5 naming defect.
- **D76's same-card duplicate pin re-pins to 235, licensed by D85 (B5c).** All five vanished duplicates are one class: `Step-ups (KB)` printed as the day's Main lift AND again in `Leg superset A`, on five `home_basic/advanced/run_half/seed 11` Tuesday legs cards in weeks 10–11. Item count 7 → 7, sections 4 → 4, cardio and title byte-identical. **Not masked** — B5c keys on the lowercase name across the whole card and ignores section labels entirely, so the `Leg superset A` → `Leg superset B` move cannot hide anything from it. **Not lost work** — the item that left is byte-identical to the Main lift that remains at higher intensity, and the card went from zero hinge and zero hip extension to keeping its only hinge. The pin stays an equality.
- **E5 is re-pinned, not deleted (D84's confinement under D85).** Deleting an assertion whose premise a later ruling superseded is an unruled removal. It now pins a `sha256` of `capSessionBudget`'s own slice — the D85-licensed digest on the candidate, the pre-D85 digest accepted only when the artifact reads `ia-version < 198`. Proof that it is still a confinement: a **comment-only** edit to the function trips it.
- **THE TRADE, ruled explicitly so it is never discovered later as a regression.** 394 days lose the whole unilateral leg block (`Leg superset A` empties) to keep a posterior item. Coach ruled hip extension the better prescription for a running build; Mario concurred and ordered it recorded as a trade, with **D90** to revisit unilateral coverage on the POOL or COST side — **never as another floor, because every floor displaces the trim.**
- **A measure pass runs BEFORE the ruling, and it is allowed to break the ruling (standing, re-proved).** D85 was ruled and concurred before its measure pass existed. The measure then falsified two of its three premises, and coach's re-audit retracted a third (the `P.drop` diagnosis). Nothing was built until the ruling matched the evidence.

'''
s=rep('## 11f. Standing decisions — do not re-derive\n','## 11f. Standing decisions — do not re-derive\n'+S11F,'11f')

